{
 "id": "03-s03-first-echo",
 "text": "Listen. Every time you make a sound, part of it travels outward. When those sound waves encounter a surface, some of their energy reflects back toward you. A wall. A doorway. A large piece of furniture. Each changes the sound in a different way. And if you learn to recognize those changes, echoes can become clues about the space around you. There's a name for this. Echolocation.",
 "seconds": 25.76,
